# Cloudflare Pages: no rewrite rules.
#
# Until T4 this file ended with `/*  /index.html  200`, which was correct while
# `/index.html` was a React shell that owned client-side routes. That shell is
# gone: every URL on this site is a directory with a real index.html, and
# Cloudflare serves it without help. Keeping the catch-all now would answer 200
# with the homepage to every address that does not exist, which is how a
# storefront collects infinite duplicate pages in a search index.
#
# A missing page should be a 404. Do not add a fallback here without deciding
# that a URL that never existed is a page.
